WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.450 --> 00:00:05.370
Let's go next to Adrian from San Francisco,
California.

00:00:05.370 --> 00:00:06.370
Hello.

00:00:06.370 --> 00:00:08.780
Hello, David, can you hear me?

00:00:08.780 --> 00:00:12.480
I can't, and you are you're not calling in
from San Francisco, Argentina.

00:00:12.480 --> 00:00:15.169
Right, or San Francisco, California.

00:00:15.169 --> 00:00:17.380
I didn't even know there was one in Argentina.

00:00:17.380 --> 00:00:18.380
Many people don't.

00:00:18.380 --> 00:00:20.340
Today, many people don't.

00:00:20.340 --> 00:00:25.420
David, I want to ask you about what are your
thoughts on having U.S. troops in the Middle

00:00:25.420 --> 00:00:30.160
East seeing there have been a recent delay
in removing troops from Afghanistan?

00:00:30.160 --> 00:00:34.980
I'm asking because there's one hypothesis
where, you know, troops are necessary to stabilize

00:00:34.980 --> 00:00:36.970
the area and prevent insurgencies.

00:00:36.970 --> 00:00:41.500
But I'm really curious to see if you think
we even have an obligation in the first place

00:00:41.500 --> 00:00:44.190
seeing the cost of American lives and capital.

00:00:44.190 --> 00:00:45.190
Yeah.

00:00:45.190 --> 00:00:50.050
So we've been talking about this really for
almost two full decades.

00:00:50.050 --> 00:00:51.200
That that's the right.

00:00:51.200 --> 00:00:55.440
I mean, the question fundamentally is that
of responsibility.

00:00:55.440 --> 00:00:58.760
If we cause a problem in the
Middle East, how

00:00:58.760 --> 00:01:06.009
long do we have a responsibility to stay for
so-called peacekeeping purposes and stabilization

00:01:06.009 --> 00:01:07.200
purposes?

00:01:07.200 --> 00:01:08.500
I have no clue.

00:01:08.500 --> 00:01:10.119
I don't know what the answer is.

00:01:10.119 --> 00:01:15.009
And, you know, we're we're in some of these
countries because of decisions made multiple

00:01:15.009 --> 00:01:17.909
presidents ago by George W. Bush does.

00:01:17.909 --> 00:01:24.619
But where does Joe Biden's responsibility
go for the destabilization that George W.

00:01:24.619 --> 00:01:27.520
Bush to George Bush's decisions brought to
the Middle East?

00:01:27.520 --> 00:01:29.500
I do not know what the answer is.

00:01:29.500 --> 00:01:35.329
I think that at a certain point you can make
the case that if you say ahead of time to

00:01:35.329 --> 00:01:39.100
the world community and to everyone involved.

00:01:39.100 --> 00:01:45.409
We understand our role in creating the situation
that was many presidents ago and much foreign

00:01:45.409 --> 00:01:51.259
policy ago, we are announcing that every troop
will be gone by X date.

00:01:51.259 --> 00:01:54.409
Let's work together to figure out how to make
that a reality reality.

00:01:54.409 --> 00:01:56.400
But the U.S. is getting out, period.

00:01:56.400 --> 00:01:57.929
And then you figure out what to do.

00:01:57.929 --> 00:02:01.740
I would think that that is that is at some
point has to be morally acceptable.

00:02:01.740 --> 00:02:06.200
But your question of if you broke it, how
long do you have a responsibility to continue

00:02:06.200 --> 00:02:07.700
fixing it is a good one.

00:02:07.700 --> 00:02:09.039
And I don't know what the answer is.

00:02:09.039 --> 00:02:15.450
You know, David, you make a really interesting
parallel to reparations, the case for reparations

00:02:15.450 --> 00:02:20.010
by attorney HESI Coates, because it's the
same philosophical question of if we broke

00:02:20.010 --> 00:02:24.930
something in this case, the horrible institution
of chattel slavery right now, how long does

00:02:24.930 --> 00:02:25.930
it have to take?

00:02:25.930 --> 00:02:29.450
And so we have to, you know, morally have
the obligation, a responsibility to.

00:02:29.450 --> 00:02:34.069
Well, I think that one is a little different
and more complicated for for a few reasons.

00:02:34.069 --> 00:02:41.430
One is that there's a question as to whether
if you just throw money at individuals

00:02:41.430 --> 00:02:45.379
on the
basis that they are still affected by the

00:02:45.379 --> 00:02:50.920
way the system used to work, you're arguably
ignoring elements of the system today that

00:02:50.920 --> 00:02:53.480
still don't actually work correctly.

00:02:53.480 --> 00:02:58.290
And and some folks believe that the first
step has to be to actually reform institutions

00:02:58.290 --> 00:03:00.500
rather than than financial reparation.

00:03:00.500 --> 00:03:02.109
I mean, this is a bigger topic.

00:03:02.109 --> 00:03:04.299
It's a different topic than the one maybe
you're bringing up.

00:03:04.299 --> 00:03:07.239
But I think that it's it's even more complicated,
arguably.

00:03:07.239 --> 00:03:09.239
Yeah, it certainly is.

00:03:09.239 --> 00:03:13.560
Hey, David, I'm a first time brand new listener
to your show, so keep it up.

00:03:13.560 --> 00:03:14.560
All right.

00:03:14.560 --> 00:03:15.560
Thank you so much.

00:03:15.560 --> 00:03:16.560
Appreciate the call.

00:03:16.560 --> 00:03:17.560
Very important.

00:03:17.560 --> 00:03:19.590
Good substantive questions.

00:03:19.590 --> 00:03:19.959
Love it

